// Value prop — one paragraph, one big idea.
//
// The pitch: AI as game master, not opponent. The LLM returns strict
// JSON state updates (see open-historia/AGENTS.md → "AI as game
// engine"). Players issue natural language commands, the AI returns a
// `{ message, updates[], newEvents[], relationChanges[], updatedStorySoFar }`
// payload, and the world ticks forward.
---

<section class="oh-value">
  <div class="oh-eyebrow center">&middot;&nbsp; THE PITCH &nbsp;&middot;</div>
  <h2 class="oh-h2 center">
    The world&rsquo;s most opinionated <em>Game Master.</em>
  </h2>
  <p class="oh-value-p">
    Every Paradox game ships with hard-coded events and scripted ledgers.
    Open Historia ships with an <strong>LLM</strong>. You type
    &ldquo;invade Bohemia&rdquo; or &ldquo;send envoy to Ottoman court&rdquo;
    and the AI returns the consequences &mdash; armies move, treaties shift,
    relations decay or warm. The Game Master keeps a running summary of
    your campaign so the world remembers, turn after turn.
  </p>
  <div class="oh-value-quote">
    <span class="oh-value-quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span>
    The memory works. <em>The campaign still needs better game feel.</em>
  </div>
</section>
